    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5447" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁμός</span></b>  (B), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰ]</span>, old word equiv. to <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τις</span>,
		only in Adv. forms <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁμοῦ, ἁμῆ,
			ἁμοῖ, ἁμῶς, ἁμόθεν, ἁμόθι,</span> and in compds. as
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδαμός,</span> Hdn.Gr.<i><span class="en">
			1.169
		</span></i>. (<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sṃ-,</i>
			cf. Goth. <i>sums (some one), suman (sometime, once).</i>)</div>
